# Muerra, Trash Tactician: "at the beginning of your first main phase, add {R} or {G} for each Raccoon you control" (CR
# 505.1a). On turn three it counts only itself - Memnite is no Raccoon - and the mana is green, which with a Mountain casts
# Wandertale Mentor, a Raccoon. On turn five it counts two, and a color is chosen for each mana: one red and one green
# (its ruling). It is no mana ability (CR 605.1b), so it waits on the stack: the pool is empty until it resolves.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Muerra, Trash Tactician
Memnite
Wandertale Mentor
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Muerra, Trash Tactician.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Stack.Count = 1
? Bot1.Mana = 
Bot1.Colors(Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {R}{G}
Bot1.Hand.Wandertale Mentor.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Colors(Red; Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Wandertale Mentor.Activate(Color: Green)
? Bot1.Mana = {R}{G}{G}

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Wandertale Mentor.Power = 2
